Subject: [PATCH 24/24] media: venus: stop startup when load scaling fails

Propagate a failed OPP, clock or interconnect vote instead of submitting
LOAD_RESOURCES and START after an unsuccessful resource setup. Unregister
buffers and free internal allocations through the existing failure labels.

This is an error-handling fix, not a demonstrated explanation for the
SM8150 encoder/RPMh timeout seen in another CPU-frequency worker.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 747c388..2909226 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -1646,7 +1646,9 @@ int venus_helper_vb2_start_streaming(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_bufs_free;
 
-	venus_pm_load_scale(inst);
+	ret = venus_pm_load_scale(inst);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_unreg_bufs;
 
 	ret = hfi_session_load_res(inst);
 	if (ret)
